The equivalence with unit normalization follows directly: $\begin{aligned}\braket{A}{A}
&=(\alpha_u^*\bra{u}+\alpha_d^*\bra{d})
  (\alpha_u\ket{u}+\alpha_d\ket{d})\\
&=|\alpha_u|^2\braket{u}{u}
 +\alpha_u^*\alpha_d\braket{u}{d}\\
&\quad +\alpha_d^*\alpha_u\braket{d}{u}
 +|\alpha_d|^2\braket{d}{d}\\
&=|\alpha_u|^2+|\alpha_d|^2=1.\end{aligned}$ Thus a physical pure state is represented by a normalized vector.

