p.src:
Use $\ket{u}=\frac{\ket{r}+\ket{l}}{\sqrt2},\qquad
\ket{d}=\frac{\ket{r}-\ket{l}}{\sqrt2}$ in the in-state: $\begin{aligned}\ket{i}
&=\frac1{\sqrt2}
\left(
\frac{\ket{r}+\ket{l}}{\sqrt2}
+i\frac{\ket{r}-\ket{l}}{\sqrt2}
\right)\\
&=\frac{1+i}{2}\ket{r}
 +\frac{1-i}{2}\ket{l}.
\end{aligned}$ Although neither coefficient visibly contains $1/\sqrt2$, $\left|\frac{1+i}{2}\right|^2
=\left|\frac{1-i}{2}\right|^2
=\frac12.$

