A convenient representative makes the relation explicit: $\ket{\psi(\theta,\phi)}
=\cos\frac{\theta}{2}\,\ket{u}
+e^{i\phi}\sin\frac{\theta}{2}\,\ket{d}.$  (Editorial clarification: Equation [eq:bloch-parameterization] is the standard normalized representative of the two-parameter family identified by the lecture. The explicit half-angle form is included to make the parameter count concrete; its dynamical and rotational interpretation belongs to later lectures.)

